                        "entry_id": "52044a9c-77ff-3582-8ef1-198cc3290db1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having tunnel vision; unable to see what is happening around one; narrow-minded."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f10652f0-b0de-4b9f-98b6-fd49762a686d",
                                "sense_id": "bcde0fe9-7f70-3e0b-9fd7-1d97bdcab191",
                                "text": "But Delhi's blinkered Kashmir policy since partition in 1947—ignoring UN demands for a self-determination plebiscite, rigging elections, manipulating or overthrowing elected governments, and neglecting economic development—lies at the heart of the problem, according to Barbara Crossette, writing in the Nation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfbd9fad-d007-486f-9dff-770fed84dcb3",
                                "sense_id": "bcde0fe9-7f70-3e0b-9fd7-1d97bdcab191",
                                "text": "Hungry for fame and the approval of rare-animal collector Queen Victoria (Imelda Staunton), Darwin deceives the Captain and his crew into believing they can get enough booty to win the pirate competition by entering Polly in a science fair. So the pirates journey to London in cheerful, blinkered defiance of the Queen, a hotheaded schemer whose royal crest reads simply “I hate pirates.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
